menu "PhoneUse: HID device"

    config PHONEUSE_HID_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the Bluetooth LE HID mouse + keyboard"
        default y
        depends on BT_BLE_ENABLED
        help
            Off: the HID commands stay in the protocol but answer "ERR not_connected", and no
            BLE HID device is advertised. Used by the HFP call audio test (sdkconfig.hfp_test),
            which runs the controller in Classic BT only mode.

    config PHONEUSE_HID_DEVICE_NAME
        string "Bluetooth device name shown on the iPhone"
        default "Oh My Phone Use HID"
        help
            Advertised in the scan response and used for the GAP device name.
            Keep it short (<= 20 characters) so it fits in the scan response.

    config PHONEUSE_HID_REPORT_INTERVAL_MS
        int "Minimum gap between consecutive HID reports (ms)"
        range 0 100
        default 8
        help
            Delay inserted after every input report (each step of a split MOVE, each
            key press and release). Keeps the BLE link from congesting and gives the
            host a steady, predictable event rate. 0 disables the delay.

    config PHONEUSE_HID_MOUSE_MAX_STEP
        int "Largest relative mouse delta sent in one report"
        range 1 127
        default 127
        help
            hid_move()/hid_scroll() split larger movements into several reports of at
            most this size. iOS applies pointer acceleration per report, so smaller
            steps give slower but more linear pointer travel.

    config PHONEUSE_HID_BLE_MITM
        bool "Require authenticated (MITM) pairing with numeric comparison"
        default n
        help
            Off: "Just Works" LE Secure Connections bonding - the iPhone shows a plain
            pairing prompt. This is what the iOS-tested reference projects use.
            On: numeric-comparison pairing; the iPhone shows a 6-digit code which this
            firmware auto-confirms. Try this if a future iOS version refuses unauthenticated
            HID pairing.

endmenu
